{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/Dockerfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:15:47.944656Z","id":"0ba27f1798c526b545dac06bd145a6286f0af23c8d9d54ab2daeb3ddf29449ee","body":{"detail":"No container runtime was available when deploy/Dockerfile was written; the stages (pnpm web build, cargo build --release -p clax-fleet, Debian runtime) are unverified, as is whether the .dockerignore leaves every file the web build and clax-embedded's build script read. Build it once: docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile .","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":38},"content_hash":"0dbe9a596ae916099226fc9b36051408fdb406390f70cd607e03a2f22e47e92b"},"summary":"The image has not been built","tags":["test-coverage","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/Dockerfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:36:07.215065Z","id":"d41bf829a13df76a20214c8703e7ffec0ae4ad6da1d56fad9d15947cef131484","body":{"detail":"Both build stages start with `COPY . .`, so any change to any file in the context invalidates the pnpm install layer (line 14) and the cargo build layer (21-22), and neither uses a cache mount, so each build downloads every crate and compiles clax-fleet and its dependencies from nothing. The context is also the whole repository (apps/, plugins/, docs/ …), less what .dockerignore leaves out, so a docs edit forces a full rebuild.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":10},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"9f4ed3636286f12bdc8e03e897550aae5074b352545d49055e037000ed42d696"},"suggested_fix":"Copy web/package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml and the workspace files first and run `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` before copying the rest; use `RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/usr/local/cargo/registry --mount=type=cache,target=/src/target` (and a pnpm store cache) for the builds; widen .dockerignore to directories the image does not read (apps/, docs/, plugins/).","summary":"Every image build reinstalls the web dependencies and rebuilds the whole Rust workspace from scratch","tags":["review","review:k8s-deep","devops","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/Dockerfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:41:21.162447Z","id":"fa5e2f93c150e636534973c917104d0bb1d57a7c57401ebfa585164bea6e0c02","body":{"detail":"deploy/Dockerfile:14-15 and 20-23: each build stage runs COPY . . before RUN pnpm install / cargo build, so any change to the context invalidates those layers (https://docs.docker.com/build/cache/#how-the-build-cache-works), and no RUN uses --mount=type=cache. .dockerignore excludes only build outputs (.git, target, node_modules, bazel-*, web/dist, apps/clax_app/build, …), not apps/, docs/ or plugins/.","kind":"comment","references":"d41bf829a13df76a20214c8703e7ffec0ae4ad6da1d56fad9d15947cef131484","summary":"confirmed: COPY . . precedes both install/build steps, with no cache mounts","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/Dockerfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:00:21.437833Z","id":"abddf1181bf1de6c2d9a753530bd67af46058df9cea5628c35cac22afeae7216","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:347050368","summary":"deploy/Dockerfile installs web dependencies in a layer of their own and uses cache mounts for pnpm's store, cargo's registry and target; .dockerignore leaves out apps/, the Worker, demo/, design/, deploy/k8s and docs but legal/ and contract.md. The image has still not been built (record 0ba27f1798).","supersedes":"d41bf829a13df76a20214c8703e7ffec0ae4ad6da1d56fad9d15947cef131484","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/Dockerfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:06:57.772601Z","id":"e8ea8aa8eccf530f144df800f505e9badb550b292f073887564bec549ac665ef","body":{"detail":"Failure: `docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile .` fails at `RUN scripts/build-web.sh` with \"Can't locate File/Find.pm in @INC\". scripts/build-web.sh runs `perl -MFile::Find -MDigest::SHA -MTime::HiRes=stat` before `pnpm run build` and `perl -MDigest::SHA -MTime::HiRes=utime` after. node:*-bookworm-slim is debian:bookworm-slim plus Node (https://github.com/nodejs/docker-node/blob/main/22/bookworm-slim/Dockerfile installs no perl, and purges what it installs), so only perl-base is present, and Debian bookworm's perl-base ships none of File/Find.pm, Digest/SHA.pm or Time/HiRes.pm (https://packages.debian.org/bookworm/amd64/perl-base/filelist). Open record 0ba27f17 notes the image was never built; this is a concrete failure it would hit.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":16},"end":{"line":23},"content_hash":"cc0926e8931ccd10c9f17601b1f958a826239cb859b3d876568c55c2ded5953e"},"suggested_fix":"In the web stage either `apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends perl` (perl-modules carries the three) before running scripts/build-web.sh, or run `cd web && pnpm run build` directly: the mtime restoring build-web.sh does serves incremental local cargo builds, not a fresh image layer. Then build the image once (record 0ba27f17).","summary":"The web stage runs scripts/build-web.sh, whose perl one-liners need File::Find, Digest::SHA and Time::HiRes, which node:22-bookworm-slim does not have","tags":["review","review:k8s-deep-2","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/Dockerfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:06:57.772830Z","id":"70cae0173c0046708f89b42bd9042afa2bcc863abc1e68f218fdfb245a97ad37","body":{"detail":"BuildKit cache mounts are keyed by `id`, which defaults to the target path, not the platform (https://docs.docker.com/reference/dockerfile/#run---mounttypecache), with sharing=shared by default. fleet-image.yml builds linux/amd64 and linux/arm64 in one buildx run, so both stages mount the same /src/target: cargo's directory lock serialises the builds, but the lock is released before `install -m 0755 target/release/clax-fleet /clax-fleet` runs, so the other platform's cargo can replace target/release/clax-fleet in between and an image gets the other architecture's binary. Each platform's build also invalidates the other's artifacts, so the cache saves little.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":34},"content_hash":"5657ece32ce48ab6b658d53ed7d940e0a9a001891719aa413e3bfa01862fe68a"},"suggested_fix":"Scope the mounts by platform: `ARG TARGETPLATFORM` and `--mount=type=cache,id=cargo-target-$TARGETPLATFORM,target=/src/target,sharing=locked` (and likewise for the registry with sharing=locked).","summary":"The cargo target cache mount is shared by both platforms of a multi-platform build, so the arm64 and amd64 builds race in one target directory","tags":["review","review:k8s-deep-2","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/Dockerfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:14.035849Z","id":"00cd3637455cd8055954294d3ab262bae0ae00fd8946c0dccd36ff2bbeb9baa3","body":{"detail":"deploy/Dockerfile:16 bases the web stage on node:22.22.0-bookworm-slim and :23 runs scripts/build-web.sh; no apt-get install in that stage. scripts/build-web.sh:17 runs `perl -MFile::Find -MDigest::SHA -MTime::HiRes=stat` and :24 `perl -MDigest::SHA -MTime::HiRes=utime`. https://packages.debian.org/bookworm/amd64/perl-base/filelist lists under File/ only Basename.pm, Glob.pm, Path.pm, Spec.pm, Spec/Unix.pm and Temp.pm, and no path containing Digest or HiRes. https://github.com/nodejs/docker-node/blob/main/22/bookworm-slim/Dockerfile never installs perl (it installs ca-certificates, curl, wget, gnupg, dirmngr, xz-utils, libatomic1 and purges the build tools). So the first perl invocation dies with \"Can't locate File/Find.pm in @INC\" and, under `set -euo pipefail` (build-web.sh:11), the RUN fails. Not run (no docker on this host).","kind":"comment","references":"e8ea8aa8eccf530f144df800f505e9badb550b292f073887564bec549ac665ef","summary":"confirmed: the web stage's base has only perl-base, which lacks File::Find, Digest::SHA and Time::HiRes that build-web.sh loads","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/Dockerfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:14.038032Z","id":"d3138d9562f72d6146cefbf09aea75ab436146e54ada2e9d52d325f1f089d053","body":{"detail":"deploy/Dockerfile:31-34: `RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/usr/local/cargo/registry --mount=type=cache,target=/src/target cargo build --release --locked -p clax-fleet && install -m 0755 target/release/clax-fleet /clax-fleet`, no id= and no sharing=. https://docs.docker.com/reference/dockerfile/#run---mounttypecache: id defaults to the target, sharing defaults to shared. .github/workflows/fleet-image.yml:38 builds both platforms in one buildx run. cargo's build-directory lock is released when cargo exits, before `install` runs, so another platform's cargo can rewrite target/release/clax-fleet in between. Fix: id=cargo-target-$TARGETPLATFORM (ARG TARGETPLATFORM).","kind":"comment","references":"70cae0173c0046708f89b42bd9042afa2bcc863abc1e68f218fdfb245a97ad37","summary":"confirmed: the /src/target cache mount has no id or platform key, so amd64 and arm64 builds share it and the install can copy the other platform's binary","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/Dockerfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T04:09:41.729613Z","id":"72b16b0bac9ed7a25324d30dcb4c66f19dfc796220c1fae5797dbc8d41d654c8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e6b59f7af","summary":"The web stage runs `cd web && pnpm run build` instead of scripts/build-web.sh, whose perl modules the slim image lacks. The image was not built here (no docker). Evidence: `just ci` at e6b59f7af passes the clax-fleet, clax-pagevfs, scripts and manifest tests (357 of 361; the 4 failures are clax-server api_seats::load_150_people_on_100_seats and //apps/clax_app:apk_test, which fail on main too, and two web e2e lanes that passed when rerun alone). PostgreSQL tests are ignored without CLAX_TEST_PG_URL.","supersedes":"e8ea8aa8eccf530f144df800f505e9badb550b292f073887564bec549ac665ef","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/Dockerfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T04:09:41.814950Z","id":"54b17c69cedbac59d96b9822ad46222d5d31acc126c5b25724ad4309cac53e0a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e6b59f7af","summary":"Both cargo cache mounts are keyed by $TARGETPLATFORM with sharing=locked, and each platform has its own GHA cache scope. Evidence: `just ci` at e6b59f7af passes the clax-fleet, clax-pagevfs, scripts and manifest tests (357 of 361; the 4 failures are clax-server api_seats::load_150_people_on_100_seats and //apps/clax_app:apk_test, which fail on main too, and two web e2e lanes that passed when rerun alone). PostgreSQL tests are ignored without CLAX_TEST_PG_URL.","supersedes":"70cae0173c0046708f89b42bd9042afa2bcc863abc1e68f218fdfb245a97ad37","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/Dockerfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T04:09:42.639021Z","id":"c10e221d37823e3dd573c1279423e70e84dd90f2eb9968d9b50e1f901864bf26","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5045811c4","summary":"Built at 5045811c4 with Docker 29.9.2 (`docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile --build-arg CLAX_BUILD_COMMIT=$(git rev-parse HEAD) -t clax-fleet:dev .`, 245MB; the build first failed because node 22's Corepack cannot start pnpm 12, fixed in 5045811c4 by installing packageManager's pnpm from npm). `clax-fleet check-catalog` passes on deploy/k8s/base/fleet.toml. `clax-fleet serve` on the PostgreSQL backend against postgres:17 migrated, answered /healthz, /readyz and /metrics 200 and /status without the key 403 on 7481, started the instance (epoch 1) on a request for its host, and /status on 127.0.0.1:7482 reported its build commit. Only linux/arm64 (this host) was built; the workflow's amd64 job has not run.","supersedes":"0ba27f1798c526b545dac06bd145a6286f0af23c8d9d54ab2daeb3ddf29449ee","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
